## Visual pack

The pictures and icons of this style are files. Use them as they are, or read them as a specification and draw your own in the same language.

| File | Content |
|---|---|
{{#each pack.files}}
| [`pack/{{file}}`](./pack/{{file}}) | {{what}} |
{{/each}}

- **Icons:** {{pack.icon.mode}}, stroke {{pack.icon.stroke_width}} on a 24px field, {{pack.icon.linecap}} caps, {{pack.icon.linejoin}} joins, container: {{pack.icon.container}}. Use: `<svg class="icon"><use href="pack/icons.svg#{{pack.first_icon}}"/></svg>`. An icon takes `currentColor`.
- **Icon family:** the sprite is cut from {{pack.icon_pack.name}} ({{pack.icon_pack.variant}}) by {{pack.icon_pack.author}}, licence {{pack.icon_pack.license}}. Reason: {{pack.icon_pack.why}} It is an open-source stand-in for a demo. For a product, use the icon library of the brand and choose the family by the rules below.
- **Display type:** weight {{pack.type.display_weight}}, tracking {{pack.type.display_tracking}}, leading {{pack.type.display_leading}}, case: {{pack.type.display_case}}.
- **Weights:** display {{pack.type.display_weight}}, subhead {{pack.type.subhead_weight}}, body {{pack.type.body_weight}}, bold in text {{pack.type.strong_weight}}, labels and buttons {{pack.type.label_weight}}. The style uses {{pack.weights.count}} weights ({{pack.weights.list}}) and no other. {{pack.weights.step}}. The accent is {{pack.weights.accent}}.
- **Body type:** {{pack.type.body_size}}, leading {{pack.type.body_leading}}.
- **Page:** hero {{pack.layout.hero}}, {{pack.layout.align}} aligned, {{pack.layout.density}} density, accent tilt {{pack.layout.tilt_deg}}°.
{{#if pack.ground}}
- **Ground:** {{pack.ground.kind}}. {{pack.ground.why}} Put the class `ground` on the first screen of the page; it takes `--ground`, a stack of gradients built from the colour tokens. The ground can run behind the copy, so put the class `ground-copy` on each text block of that screen: the block gets `--color-bg` and a soft edge. Keep the rest of the page on `--color-bg`.
{{/if}}
- **Text colour:** `--color-text` is for the main reading field only. On each field, use its token: `--color-on-bg`, `--color-on-surface`, `--color-on-primary`, `--color-on-accent`.

